ec or config.\n- module Producer :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Producer :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Consumer :: init: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Consumer :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- refinement obligation: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\nFirst error line: Parsing or semantic analysis failed.\n\nLast bundle slug: producer_consumer_system\nParent module: ProducerConsumerSystem\nModules: BoundedQueue(abs), BoundedQueue(impl), Producer(abs), Producer(impl), Consumer(abs), Consumer(impl)\nRevise the failing module(s) and/or abstraction map(s). Return one call to repair_module_bundle with the FULL revised bundle."}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WNbiTovHhLQK4PeqsMNoEw', 'name': 'repair_module_bundle', 'input': {'reasoning': "Parse errors persist across all modules. The likely culprit is `UNION { [1..k -> 1..MaxItem] : k \\in 0..Capacity }` — TLA+ requires the set-comprehension `UNION` form to use proper syntax. Actually the bigger issue is probably the `RECURSIVE SumSeq(_)` followed by `SumSeq(s) == ...` outside a LET — that needs to be on its own line correctly. But the BoundedQueue_Abs has no RECURSIVE and still fails parse. Let me check — the `\\\\A i \\\\in 1..Len(queue) : queue[i] \\\\in 1..MaxItem` should be fine. The parent module references `Q!Inv` etc which is fine but the parent INSTANCEs `BoundedQueue_Impl` which has `UNION { [...] : k \\in ... }`. That syntax IS valid TLA+. Actually wait, BoundedQueue_Abs has no UNION and it ALSO fails. Look again: `Inv == /\\\\ Len(queue) \\\\in 0..Capacity /\\\\ \\\\A i \\\\in 1..Len(queue) : queue[i] \\\\in 1..MaxItem`. This is at top-level; the `\\\\A` has lower precedence and needs parens, otherwise it gets parsed strangely. Let me parenthesize. Same for Producer. Also, `[1..k -> 1..MaxItem]` is the function set notation, which IS valid. But `UNION {set : k \\in S}` produces a set of sets, then UNION flattens — valid. Let me try without UNION, just use a direct bound: `received \\in [DOMAIN received -> 1..MaxItem]` — but TLC needs an explicit type. Use `Seq` won't work. Best: use `IsFiniteSet`-style by enumerating via `\\E k \\in 0..MaxLen : received \\in [1..k -> 1..MaxItem]`. Actually, the cleanest fix: write `\\A i \\in DOMAIN received : received[i] \\in 1..MaxItem` as the bound, but TLC needs to enumerate states. Without a bounded type for the sequence variable, TLC can't enumerate initial states for consec/property checks if Init is the Inv. But we're passing Inv as init for the consec check — it must enumerate. So we DO need bounded set. Let me try `\\E k \\in 0..MaxLen : received \\in [1..k -> 1..MaxItem]`.\n\nActually the issue may simply be that `UNION { [1..k -> 1..MaxItem] : k \\in 0..Capacity }` IS parsed but creates a set that includes the empty function `[1..0 -> S]`. Let me re-examine more carefully — the parse error is the issue. Let me wrap the \\A in parens.", 'targeted_failure': 'parse errors all modules', 'slug': 'producer_consumer_system', 'parent': {'name': 'ProducerConsumerSystem', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE ProducerConsumerSystem ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nVARIABLES buffer, generated, nextItem, received, sum, pcQ, pcP, pcC\n\nQ == INSTANCE BoundedQueue_Impl WITH buffer <- buffer, pc <- pcQ\nP == INSTANCE Producer_Impl WITH generated <- generated, nextItem <- nextItem, pc <- pcP\nC == INSTANCE Consumer_Impl WITH received <- received, sum <- sum, pc <- pcC\n\nSpec == Q!Spec /\\ P!Spec /\\ C!Spec\n\nIsPrefix(s, t) == (Len(s) <= Len(t)) /\\ (\\A i \\in 1..Len(s) : s[i] = t[i])\n\nRECURSIVE SumSeq(_)\nSumSeq(s) == IF Len(s) = 0 THEN 0 ELSE Head(s) + SumSeq(Tail(s))\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ Q!Inv\n  /\\ P!Inv\n  /\\ C!Inv\n  /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..3\n  /\\ IsPrefix(received, generated)\n  /\\ received \\o buffer = generated\n  /\\ sum = SumSeq(received)\n  /\\ nextItem \\in 1..4\n\nProperty ==\n  /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..3\n  /\\ IsPrefix(received, generated)\n  /\\ nextItem <= 4\n\n===='}, 'modules': [{'name': 'BoundedQueue', 'role': 'abs', 'tla_source': "---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANTS Capacity, MaxItem\n\nVARIABLE queue\n\nvars == <<queue>>\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..k -> 1..MaxItem] : k \\in 0..Capacity }\n\nInit == queue = <<>>\n\nEnqueue(x) ==\n  /\\ x \\in 1..MaxItem\n  /\\ Len(queue) < Capacity\n  /\\ queue' = Append(queue, x)\n\nDequeue ==\n  /\\ Len(queue) > 0\n  /\\ queue' = Tail(queue)\n\nNext == (\\E x \\in 1..MaxItem : Enqueue(x)) \\/ Dequeue\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ queue \\in BoundedSeqs\n  /\\ Len(queue) \\in 0..Capacity\n\nProperty == Len(queue) \\in 0..Capacity\n\n===="}, {'name': 'BoundedQueue', 'role': 'impl', 'abstraction_map': {'queue': 'buffer'}, 'tla_source': '---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANTS Capacity, MaxItem\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..k -> 1..MaxItem] : k \\in 0..Capacity }\n\n(* --algorithm BoundedQueue\nvariables buffer = <<>>;\n\nbegin\nLoop:\n  while TRUE do\n    either\n      with x \\in 1..MaxItem do\n        if Len(buffer) < Capacity then\n          buffer := Append(buffer, x);\n        end if;\n      end with;\n    or\n      if Len(buffer) > 0 then\n        buffer := Tail(buffer);\n      end if;\n    end either;\n  end while;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ buffer \\in BoundedSeqs\n  /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n  /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Done"}\n\nProperty == Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n\n====', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANTS Capacity, MaxItem\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..k -> 1..MaxItem] : k \\in 0..Capacity }\n\n(* --algorithm BoundedQueue\nvariables buffer = <<>>;\n\nbegin\nLoop:\n  while TRUE do\n    either\n      with x \\in 1..MaxItem do\n        if Len(buffer) < Capacity then\n          buffer := Append(buffer, x);\n        end if;\n      end with;\n    or\n      if Len(buffer) > 0 then\n        buffer := Tail(buffer);\n      end if;\n    end either;\n  end while;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ buffer \\in BoundedSeqs\n  /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n  /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Done"}\n\nProperty == Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n\n====', 'constants': {'values': {'Capacity': [3], 'MaxItem': [10]}}}, {'name': 'Producer', 'role': 'abs', 'tla_source': "---- MODULE Producer_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANTS MaxProduce\n\nVARIABLES generated, nextItem\n\nvars == <<generated, nextItem>>\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..k -> 1..MaxProduce] : k \\in 0..MaxProduce }\n\nInit ==\n  /\\ generated = <<>>\n  /\\ nextItem = 1\n\nProduce ==\n  /\\ nextItem <= MaxProduce\n  /\\ generated' = Append(generated, nextItem)\n  /\\ nextItem' = nextItem + 1\n\nNext == Produce\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ nextItem \\in 1..(MaxProduce+1)\n  /\\ generated \\in BoundedSeqs\n  /\\ Len(generated) = nextItem - 1\n  /\\ \\A i \\in 1..Len(generated) : generated[i] = i\n\nProperty == nextItem <= MaxProduce + 1\n\n===="}, {'name': 'Producer', 'role': 'impl', 'abstraction_map': {'generated': 'generated'